---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const updated = '2026-11-22';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="What soloyolo's calculators and document generators can and cannot tell you, how the tax sources are checked, and where your responsibility starts."
  path="/disclaimer/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Disclaimer' }]} />

    <article class="max-w-3xl pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.1rem,1.4rem+3.4vw,3.4rem)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        Disclaimer
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
        Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>
      </p>

      <div class="prose-ledger mt-10">
        <p>
          soloyolo provides free, browser-based business calculators and document generators. The
          output is arithmetic and formatting, not professional advice. This page explains the
          boundary so you know what to check before you rely on a number or send a document.
        </p>

        <h2>Not tax, legal, accounting or financial advice</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site is tax, legal, accounting, investment or financial advice, and using
          the site does not create a professional relationship. The tools do not know your
          residency, entity structure, registrations, deductions, exemptions, treaty position or the
          facts of a particular client. Those facts decide whether a rate, a tax treatment or a
          document is right for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before you send an invoice, charge a tax rate or rely on a calculation, check the rule
          with the tax authority in your country or a qualified accountant or lawyer. The country
          guides link the official sources the site used.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy and sources</h2>
        <p>
          The formulas are covered by automated tests, and worked examples on the pages are computed
          by the same engine the tool uses. Country-specific claims are checked against an official
          source and carry the date they were last verified. Tax rates, thresholds, invoice
          requirements and e-invoicing rules change; a page that was correct on its verification
          date may be out of date today.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every figure is informational output. You remain responsible for the document you issue,
          the tax you charge and the return you file.
        </p>

        <h2>Documents and print output</h2>
        <p>
          The generators produce a printable document in your browser. They are not an e-invoicing
          integration, do not submit anything to a tax authority, and do not clear an invoice
          through a government portal. Where a market requires structured e-invoicing or a clearance
          step, the country guide says so and the tool does not claim compliance.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          Links to government, tax authority and other official pages are provided so you can check
          the primary source. Those sites are outside our control; their content and availability
          can change. A link is not an endorsement of everything on the destination site.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The site is funded by advertising. Ads are labelled, kept out of calculator workflows and
          never change a formula or a result. Advertising is not advice, and an ad appearing next to
          a page does not mean the advertiser endorses or has reviewed that page. See the
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how ad cookies work and how to turn ads off.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          The site and its tools are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
          kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. To the maximum
          extent permitted by law, {SITE.operator} is not liable for any loss arising from use of
          the site or reliance on its output, including lost profit, lost business, penalties,
          mispriced work or an incorrectly issued document. Nothing in this disclaimer limits
          liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Found a wrong number, a stale rate or a broken source link? Write to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> and include the page and
          the official source you would like the page to reflect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
